ESE WILL HELP YOU DETERMINE WHAT    SHIFT VALUES ARE RIGHT FOR THE    DATA YOU WANT. Á SHIFT OF 0 IS OF    COURSEETHE SAME AS NO SHIFT.  ÎUMBER OF ÃYCLES: ÔHIS DETERMINES    HOW MANY CYCLES OF THE PATTERN YOU    WANT TO GENERATE. ÉF YOU CHOOSE 1    CYCLE, YOU WILL GET ONE COMPLETE    180 DEGREE CHUNK OF DATA, WHICH IS    THE COMPLETE PATTERN DISPLAYED.    ÃHOOSING 2, 3, OR MORE CYCLES WILL    GENERATE THAT MANY CHUNKS OF THE    SAME PATTERN, CONSECUTIVLY IN    MEMORY AND FITTED WITHIN YOUR    HI/LO RANGE AND NUMBER OF DATA.    ÏNE CYCLE SHOULD BE USED UNLESS    YOU WANT A DENSER REPEATING SET OF    DATA.  ÁFTER ALL THAT IS ENTERED, THE DATAWILL BE GENERATED, AND YOU'LL BE ASKEDFOR A FILENAME TO SAVE THE DATA. ÈITRETURN WITHOUT ENTERING ANY FILENAMETO ABORT AND RESTART ×IX. ÏTHERWISETHE DATA IS SAVED AS SUCH:  1 BYTE DATA:        FROM $3800 - $3800+# DATA  2 BYTE DATA LO BYTES:        FROM $3800 - $3800+# DATA              HI BYTES:     FROM $3800+# DATA - $3800+2*# DATA-----ÉNDEXED ÐATTERN ÇENERATOR  ÉF YOU WANT TO USE THE INDEXEDPATTERN GENERATOR, THEN INSTEAD OFHITTING SPACE AT THE START, HIT ÒÅÔÕÒÎINSTEAD.  ÔHE INDEXED PATTERN GENERATOR WILLLET YOU SELECT 2 PATTERNS, ONE TO BEUSED AS A BASE PATTERN AND THE OTHER ASTHE INDEX PATTERN. ÔHE INDEX PATTERN ISUSED TO SELECT DATA VALUES OUT OF THEBASE DATA VALUES. ÔHEN THOSE VALUES ARESTORED AS THE ACTUAL PATTERN. ÔHISSHOULD YEILD SOME VERY STRANGE RESULTSAND ODD PATTERNS, BUT YOU'LL NEED TOEXPERIMENT TO FIND WHAT YOU WANT...  ÁFTER HITTING RETURN, YOU'RE ASKEDFOR THE BASE PATTERN. ÙOU CAN HIT A-ZOR SHIFT + A-N JUST AS BEFORE, AND HITSPACE TO SELECT THE PATTERN. ÔHENYOU'RE ASKED THE SAME INFORMATION ASIF YOU WERE GENERATING A SINGLEPATTERN - HI/LO, # DATA, INVERSION,ETC. ÁFTER THIS, THE BASE DATA WILL BEGENERATED. ÎEXT, YOU'RE ASKED FOR THEINDEX PATTERN, AND YOU SELECT IT THESAME WAY AS THE BASE PATTERN. ÂUT ONCEYOU SELECT THE INDEX, ×IX WILLIMMEDIATLY START